@startuml j12-whatsapp-check-and-other-ways
title J12 Checking a number on WhatsApp when it is added, and other ways to send (v1.2.2, v1.2.3)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam titleFontSize 17
skinparam titleFontColor #0E5C45
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #0E5C45
  LifeLineBorderColor #7FA89A
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantBorderColor #0E5C45
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ParticipantFontColor #0B3D2E
  ActorBorderColor #0E5C45
  ActorBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  ActorFontColor #0B3D2E
  GroupBorderColor #0E5C45
  GroupHeaderFontColor #0E5C45
  GroupBackgroundColor #F3F8F6
  DividerBorderColor #0E5C45
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F2EE
  DividerFontColor #0B3D2E
  BoxBorderColor #0E5C45
}
skinparam database {
  BorderColor #0E5C45
  BackgroundColor #E8F2EE
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #B08A2E
  BackgroundColor #FFF8E6
  FontSize 12
}
actor "Shop owner" as Owner
participant "Browser UI\n(index.html)" as UI
participant "app.js" as App
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "WhatsApp / SMS app" as WA
autonumber
note over App, LS : add-ons wacheck.js (v1.2.3) and sendways.js (v1.2.2),\nthrough the window.Hisaab hooks of app.js.\nNo app can ask WhatsApp beforehand whether a number\nhas an account, so the owner answers.
== Check the number when the customer is added ==
Owner -> UI : add a customer by hand (name and phone), press Add
UI -> App : onAddCustomer(): save, render()
App -> UI : under the add form (#wa-added):\n"<name> added. Check the number on WhatsApp now,\nso reminders reach them." and Check on WhatsApp
note right of App : a loaded shop file offers nothing
opt Owner taps Check on WhatsApp (#wa-added-go)
  UI -> WA : open wa.me/91<phone> with a hello message:\nname and shop, no balance
  UI -> App : the page moves to #/c/<phone>
  App -> UI : #wa-check asks\n"Did WhatsApp open a chat with this number?"
  alt the chat opened
    Owner -> UI : tap Yes (#wa-check-yes)
    UI -> LS : setItem('hisaab.wa', phone: ok and the date)
    App -> UI : "Checked: this number is on WhatsApp."
  else WhatsApp said the number is not on WhatsApp
    Owner -> UI : tap No (#wa-check-no)
    UI -> LS : setItem('hisaab.wa', phone: no and the date)
    App -> UI : "Not on WhatsApp. Send by SMS, or change the number."
    App -> UI : open "Other ways to send" (#send-ways)
  end
end
note right of UI : any customer page has Check on WhatsApp\n(#wa-check-go); the same question follows
== The reminder to a refused number ==
Owner -> UI : open the customer page
App -> UI : under the reminder buttons, the fold-out\n"Other ways to send" with the same message\nas the WhatsApp reminder (J4)
opt sample number (starts 90000001)
  App -> UI : the fold-out opens by itself, with a note\nthat the number is made up
end
alt Send as SMS (#send-sms)
  UI -> WA : open sms:+91<phone> with the message
else Choose a contact in WhatsApp (#send-pick)
  UI -> WA : open wa.me with no number;\nthe owner picks any contact
else Copy the message (#send-copy)
  UI -> UI : copy to the clipboard;\n"Message copied" for 2.5 s
end
Owner -> WA : press Send
note right of WA : the app never sends by itself
@enduml
